    3. Design 2-4 distractor sprites with distinct crops (different shape or different cell pattern). Each uses 2-4 colors, bbox 2-5 x 2-4, 5-9 fg cells.
    4. Ensure no distractor crop matches the duplicate crop (trivially satisfied by using different shapes or patterns).
    5. Place all sprites (2 copies of duplicate + distractors) on the grid with min Manhattan gap >= 2. Use rejection sampling on placement positions.
    6. Assign colors from palette of 1-9 ensuring 5-8 total distinct fg colors across all sprites.
